{
  "@context": {
    "skos": "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#",
    "dcterms": "http://purl.org/dc/terms/"
  },
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities",
      "@type": "skos:ConceptScheme",
      "skos:prefLabel": "BPMN activities, extracted (cat-harness)",
      "skos:definition": "Candidate terms extracted from every BPMN task and call activity: `name` as the label, its own `<documentation>` as the definition, the element id as the code. Generated by folio-assistant-core/scripts/glossary-extract.ts; not curated, and never hand-edited: a person promotes a term by authoring it in a glossary of their own.",
      "dcterms:source": "BPMN activities of cat-harness"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_activitylog.a_dowork",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Do the work"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The task itself. This diagram says nothing about how it is done; it only brackets it, so that a reader of the log can tell where one run of work began and ended."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_DoWork",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/activity-log.bpmn#A_DoWork",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_activitylog.a_emptyall",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Discard all entries, or a whole session"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Remove every entry, one session's, or those before a date — emptyLog with { all }, { session } or { before }; there is no default selector. A file that will not parse is kept, and the result must say what was refused and why, not only what was removed."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_EmptyAll",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/activity-log.bpmn#A_EmptyAll",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_activitylog.a_emptyone",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Discard one entry by id"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Remove one entry by its stable id, with emptyLog({ id }). Logs are the one exception to the never-delete rule because an entry records no decision; the exception covers files that declare folio-log/v1, not the directory."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_EmptyOne",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/activity-log.bpmn#A_EmptyOne",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_activitylog.a_logend",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Log task-end"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Write a task-end entry, with the outcome in the detail. The step is the unit: an entry per step, not one when the whole process finishes, or every intermediate entry is lost."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_LogEnd",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/activity-log.bpmn#A_LogEnd",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_activitylog.a_logmessage",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Log a message or an error"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Write a message or error entry whenever a later reader would need it. A command run goes in `execution` (command, exit code, where output went) — never the output itself, and never a secret, token or credential: capture on puts entries in git."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_LogMessage",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/activity-log.bpmn#A_LogMessage",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_activitylog.a_logstart",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Log task-start"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Write a task-start entry before touching anything: summary, actor, and the process/task/bean/branch/session it belongs to where they exist. role, process and task are optional on purpose — do not invent a lane for work done outside a process."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_LogStart",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/activity-log.bpmn#A_LogStart",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_activitylog.a_persistlog",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Persist the log to the data store"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Capture is explicitly on — by <cat-harness.processes:log capture=\"on\"/> on the process or by config — so the entries go to the git data store. Only this branch commits anything."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_PersistLog",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/activity-log.bpmn#A_PersistLog",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_activitylog.a_reportcapturestate",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Report the capture state"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Capture is off or unknown, so nothing is committed. Say which of the two it is: off is somebody's decision, unknown means nobody could tell, and an agent that believes it has an audit trail when it has none acts on a false belief."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_ReportCaptureState",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/activity-log.bpmn#A_ReportCaptureState",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_actorroleadministration.callactivity_codechangereview",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Branch, gates, PR and review [code-change-review]"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Called rather than restated. The mechanics of getting an edit reviewed and merged are not specific to the role graph, and a second description of them is a second thing free to disagree with the first."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "CallActivity_CodeChangeReview",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/actor-role-administration.bpmn#CallActivity_CodeChangeReview",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_actorroleadministration.task_addactor",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Add an actor, and declare its kind"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Human, agentic or mechanical. A userTask because the agentic/mechanical line is JUDGEMENT — role-model.md says so — and reading it wrong disqualifies the actor from every judgement task it exists to perform, silently."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_AddActor",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/actor-role-administration.bpmn#Task_AddActor",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_actorroleadministration.task_assignroles",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Open or close a role to an actor"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The join every other diagram depends on. An empty `roles` is a DETERMINED empty — it says the actor takes on none — and is not the same as an absent one, which asserts nothing."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_AssignRoles",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/actor-role-administration.bpmn#Task_AssignRoles",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_actorroleadministration.task_grantorrevoke",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Grant or revoke a permission"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "A permission travels with the PARTICIPANT and cross-cuts every lane, so unlike a role it cannot be scoped by the diagram it is used in. Granting one is a standing decision, which is why this lane is person-only and why the log capture on this process is on."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_GrantOrRevoke",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/actor-role-administration.bpmn#Task_GrantOrRevoke",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_actorroleadministration.task_retireactor",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Retire an actor — never delete one"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "An actor id is referenced from roles, diagrams, beans and commits, so removing the file leaves every one of those unable to tell retirement from accident. Same rule, and the same reason, as a scrapped bean."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_RetireActor",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/actor-role-administration.bpmn#Task_RetireActor",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_actorroleadministration.task_runkgaudit",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Audit the graph [kg:audit]"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "AFTER the change, not before. Every criterion here is a join — role to lane, actor to role, activity to skill — so what an administrative edit breaks is not in the file it edited. The sidecars under `test/results/kg-qa/` are committed for the reason a printed verdict is not: without them, \"unbound since it was drawn\" and \"broken by this change\" are indistinguishable."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_RunKgAudit",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/actor-role-administration.bpmn#Task_RunKgAudit",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_adjudication.a_adjudicate",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Adjudicate the disagreement"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The judgement itself, and the one step nothing here can check: if a mechanism could decide it, the process would not have been entered. It declares NO `cat-harness.processes:adjudication codes` on purpose, and that absence is the whole of bean `bvuk`. This step used to name three — stands, scope, dispensation — and six diagrams called it: `review-narrative` and `voice-review`, whose question those three answer, and four whose question they do not. `refresh-materialized` asks which side wins a local-vs-remote conflict; there is no criterion to scope there and no dispensation to grant, yet the outcome half ran regardless. Since the caller's question decides the permitted answers, the caller declares them: `cat-harness.processes:adjudication codes` on its OWN call activity, with its own gateway acting on them. `criterion-adjudication.bpmn` is that for the QA-criterion question. What could NOT be fixed by passing the codes as data, which was this bean's first recommendation: the three branches ran three different TASKS, so a caller handed `local-wins` would have had it pointing at `A_ScopeCriterion`. The branches had to move, not the enum."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_Adjudicate",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/adjudication.bpmn#A_Adjudicate",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_adjudication.a_dispatch",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Dispatch with adjudicator_sees — never the artefact"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "`UntaintedDispatch` on the criterion declares what each party is given; the caller names a subject and a criterion and does not hand-assemble a brief, because the party composing a brief by hand is the producer. `untaintedPartitionDefects` reports `overlap` when the checker and the adjudicator can read the same file — one of them is then grading its own input, and the verdict measures nothing while raising no error."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_Dispatch",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/adjudication.bpmn#A_Dispatch",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_adjudication.a_statefinding",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "State the finding and what it read"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Each provider says what it found and on what evidence. A finding that does not show what it read is an opinion, and an adjudicator cannot tell it from a finding about some other version of the block."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_StateFinding",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/adjudication.bpmn#A_StateFinding",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_atomicmassdrift.task_check",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Regenerate AtomicMass.lean&#10;from the data table &#8212; and diff"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Run gen_atomic_mass.py --check: regenerate AtomicMass.lean from the data table and diff it against the committed file. Any divergence exits 1 with a unified diff and fails the PR — a Lean file that compiles must not carry numbers the table no longer produces."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_Check",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/atomic-mass-drift-check.bpmn#Task_Check",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_beanlifecycle.task_checkexists",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Check before you create (exact-title search)"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "STRICT. `beans create` is not idempotent: it mints a fresh id every call and dedupes on nothing, so re-entering a step duplicates the plan instead of no-op'ing. In the qou folio an unguarded re-run produced 14,688 duplicate beans — 92% of every open bean — which starved the idle-backlog policy of signal and collided with 15 real ids."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_CheckExists",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn#Task_CheckExists",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_beanlifecycle.task_claim",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Claim it (status: in-progress)"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Idempotent. Claim BEFORE working, and note the branch, so a sibling session can see the item is taken rather than discovering it by collision."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_Claim",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn#Task_Claim",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_beanlifecycle.task_complete",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Complete (no unchecked todos left)"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Only once nothing is unchecked, and with a summary of what changed. The engine's `resolve` completes a bean only after the instance itself has completed — whether work is done is a judgement, and a bean is not closed on someone else's say-so."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_Complete",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn#Task_Complete",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_beanlifecycle.task_create",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Create the bean (agent CLI, not an engine op)"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "`beans create \"<title>\"`. This is the AGENT's call. The workflow engine has no `create` op — its vocabulary is claim, note and resolve, all of which act on an instance's existing bean."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_Create",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn#Task_Create",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_beanlifecycle.task_leavealone",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Leave it alone (coordinate instead)"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Never resolve, scrap or delete a bean another session or a human owns. Claiming is how two sessions avoid picking the same item; closing someone else's is how one of them loses work it had not finished reporting."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_LeaveAlone",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn#Task_LeaveAlone",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_beanlifecycle.task_recordblocker",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Record the blocker and hand back"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Blocked is not scrapped. Set `--blocked-by`, say in the body what would unblock it, and return it to `todo` so it is visible to whoever can act. An in-progress bean nobody is progressing reads as active work."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_RecordBlocker",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn#Task_RecordBlocker",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_beanlifecycle.task_scrap",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Scrap with reasons NEVER delete"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "`status: scrapped`, plus a \"Reasons for Scrapping\" section. This is what \"disable\" means here — the CLI has no disabled state; its vocabulary is draft, todo, in-progress, completed, scrapped. DELETION IS NEVER THE ANSWER, even though `beans delete` exists. A scrapped bean records that the work was considered and rejected, and why; a deleted one leaves a sibling session unable to tell abandonment from accident, and leaves the next agent free to re-open the same dead end."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_Scrap",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn#Task_Scrap",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_beanlifecycle.task_work",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Work, keeping the body current (this is 'edit')"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Editing a bean is not a separate ceremony: check off todo items as they happen, append measurements with the command and date that produced them, and record what you now know that the next agent does not. A bean whose body is a title is a placeholder, not a plan."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_Work",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn#Task_Work",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_boardopenclose.a_close",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Close the window back to its avatar"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "[x] closes the window back to its avatar. Only a person's [x] does this; a zoom-out never closes a window, or [x] and zooming become indistinguishable to the reader."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_Close",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/board-open-close.bpmn#A_Close",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_boardopenclose.a_offerwayback",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Leave a reachable way back"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Leave the way back reachable: the collapsed window becomes a control in its own position and focus moves to it — left alone, focus lands on <body> and the keyboard position is lost. An action whose inverse is not reachable is not a toggle (bean l4zi)."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_OfferWayBack",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/board-open-close.bpmn#A_OfferWayBack",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_boardopenclose.a_open",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Project a window onto the board"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Project a window onto the board for the chosen card. A window is not the card grown large: it survives zooming out, and only [x] closes it. The frame is fixed ([x] always present, always in the same place); the kind fills in its declared controls."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_Open",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/board-open-close.bpmn#A_Open",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_boardopenclose.a_raise",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Raise the window the reader selected"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Raise the selected window to the top. Selecting ANY part raises it, not just a title bar. Z-order is session-only by stated default: no z is written to the layout, so a raise is never a file write."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_Raise",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/board-open-close.bpmn#A_Raise",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_boardopenclose.a_renderavatars",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Render every card as its avatar"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Render every card as its avatar — the starting state. Each content kind controls its own avatar; the board decides only that nothing starts open."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_RenderAvatars",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/board-open-close.bpmn#A_RenderAvatars",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_boardopenclose.a_resolvethreshold",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Resolve the kind's zoom threshold"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Resolve the semantic-zoom threshold for each card's kind: the folio default unless the kind overrides it with a stated because. Return the source alongside the value, so a card that flipped too early can be traced to a decision or to a default."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_ResolveThreshold",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/board-open-close.bpmn#A_ResolveThreshold",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_boardopenclose.a_swaptoavatar",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Swap cards below the threshold; leave open windows alone"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Cards whose rendered width is strictly below the threshold swap to their avatar — automatic, driven by size. Open windows are left alone: semantic zoom and open/close are two mechanisms and must not be conflated."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_SwapToAvatar",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/board-open-close.bpmn#A_SwapToAvatar",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_boardplacenote.a_createnote",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Write the note into the folio — with no coordinate"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "A new note: write it into the folio with no x, no y, no board and no position. A folio is complete with no board, and one note may sit on several boards, which a coordinate on the note could not express."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_CreateNote",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/board-place-note.bpmn#A_CreateNote",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_boardplacenote.a_place",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Record x,y for this note on THIS board"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Record the note's x,y in the layout layer for THIS board, naming the note by id. An existing card dragged here only gets a new position — placing is not creating, so no content is duplicated."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_Place",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/board-place-note.bpmn#A_Place",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_boardplacenote.a_sweeporphans",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Sweep positions whose note is gone"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Remove every position in this board's layer whose note no longer exists. The sweep edits only the layer — one file, one pass — and never a note a person owns; a stale position must not keep a note alive."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_SweepOrphans",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/board-place-note.bpmn#A_SweepOrphans",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_boardrelocate.a_askconfirm",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Name what will move, and where it lands"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Before anything moves, name the content that would move — what it is, with its size and age — and where it lands. The confirmation sits in front of the move: an agent never relocates a durable artefact on its own initiative."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_AskConfirm",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/board-relocate.bpmn#A_AskConfirm",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_boardrelocate.a_cancel",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Leave the content exactly where it is"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The reader said no: nothing moves, no position is dropped, and the board is left exactly as it was. Drawn as its own end state because a destructive action whose refusal is not drawn gets performed by accident."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_Cancel",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/board-relocate.bpmn#A_Cancel",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_boardrelocate.a_movecontent",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Relocate the content to the trashcan"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Relocate the confirmed content — that one thing, not the class it belongs to — to the trashcan. The folio changes first, because the folio carries what is true."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_MoveContent",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/board-relocate.bpmn#A_MoveContent",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_boardrelocate.a_reportmove",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Say what moved and where it went"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Tell the reader what moved and where it went, so the content can be found in the trashcan rather than inferred missing from a card that disappeared."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_ReportMove",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/board-relocate.bpmn#A_ReportMove",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_boardrelocate.a_updatelayer",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Drop its positions and sweep orphans"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Only after the content has moved: drop its positions from the layout layer and sweep any position whose note is now gone. Sweeping first would make the board authoritative over the folio for one step."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_UpdateLayer",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/board-relocate.bpmn#A_UpdateLayer",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_buildl1kg.task_assets",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Record assets[] — local path or remote URL"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "kind / role / url-or-path / checksum / retrieved. A SIBLING of library:, never inside it: LibraryRef is regenerated from the tree, so an authored URL placed there is dropped on the next sync."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_Assets",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/ingest-build-l1-kg.bpmn#Task_Assets",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_buildl1kg.task_bind",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Bind the folder name to the bibliography slug"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Bind the folder name to the document's bibliography slug, so library/<bib-slug>/ and its citation key are the same string: a citation resolves to a directory without a lookup table between them."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_Bind",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/ingest-build-l1-kg.bpmn#Task_Bind",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_buildl1kg.task_dublin",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Write dublin-core.jsonld (the record of truth)"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "One standalone Dublin Core record per folder. dcterms is already this corpus's JSON-LD vocabulary, so this extends a live context rather than introducing one."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_Dublin",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/ingest-build-l1-kg.bpmn#Task_Dublin",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_buildl1kg.task_link",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Link L1 nodes into the corpus graph"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Anything in library/ is L1 source content. A knowledge-graph reference from any artefact -- paper, L2, L3 -- resolves to it through library/."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_Link",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/ingest-build-l1-kg.bpmn#Task_Link",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_buildl1kg.task_manifest",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Write manifest.jsonld referencing it"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Write manifest.jsonld for the folder: its @id, @type folio:SourceDocument, what it contains and its provenance, referencing the standalone dublin-core.jsonld as the record of truth rather than copying its fields."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_Manifest",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/ingest-build-l1-kg.bpmn#Task_Manifest",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_cihealth.task_check",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Run check:ci-health,&#10;WRITING the report file"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Run check:ci-health --out, writing the report file before any exit path. Exit 0 clean, 1 live failures, 2 could not check. bun also exits 1 on an uncaught exception, so an exit 1 with no report file is a crash and is treated as could-not-check."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_Check",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/ci-health-watch.bpmn#Task_Check",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_cihealth.task_close",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Close the&#10;tracking issue"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Clean: close the open ci-health issue, if any, saying why (main is clean). Runs only on a clean verdict — on unknown the issue is left untouched and the job fails instead, because could-not-check is never rendered as clean."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_Close",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/ci-health-watch.bpmn#Task_Close",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_cihealth.task_label",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Ensure the tracking&#10;label exists"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Create the ci-health label with --force so it exists before either issue path runs — the close path filters on it too, and on a repository that has never had a finding it would not exist yet. Skipped on an unknown verdict."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_Label",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/ci-health-watch.bpmn#Task_Label",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_cihealth.task_track",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Open or EDIT the one&#10;tracking issue"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Findings: EDIT the one open issue labelled ci-health if there is one, otherwise create it, with the report as the body. One issue edited in place, never a new issue or a comment per run, so the tracking issue never becomes a feed."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_Track",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/ci-health-watch.bpmn#Task_Track",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_codechangereview.task_addressreview",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Address the review"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Every finding is answered — implemented, or replied to with why not. A design question does not excuse skipping the nits in the same review."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_AddressReview",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/code-change-review.bpmn#Task_AddressReview",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_codechangereview.task_branchandannounce",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Branch, and announce it"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Announce the branch WHEN IT IS CREATED, not when the work is done. The gap between one agent's view of an issue and everyone else's is what this closes."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_BranchAndAnnounce",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/code-change-review.bpmn#Task_BranchAndAnnounce",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_codechangereview.task_claimbean",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Claim the work item"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Claim before you work. A claim ANNOUNCES rather than reserves until the PR exists, which is why the branch is announced at the next step and not at the end."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_ClaimBean",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/code-change-review.bpmn#Task_ClaimBean",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_codechangereview.task_closebean",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Record what was done, and close"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "A closed work item is read later by somebody deciding whether to reopen the subject, so \"completed\" with nothing behind it cannot be audited. An ISSUE is never closed on the agent's own say-so."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_CloseBean",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/code-change-review.bpmn#Task_CloseBean",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_codechangereview.task_commitandopenpr",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Commit, push, open the PR"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The PR opens at the FIRST commit, even on a stub, and permission is never asked for it. Holding a green PR back for someone to look at is not caution — it is a blocked reviewer."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_CommitAndOpenPR",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/code-change-review.bpmn#Task_CommitAndOpenPR",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_codechangereview.task_diagnose",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Root-cause the failure"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "\"Flake\" is not a root cause. A red PR is work now, whatever its review state — only a green, mergeable head waits on reviewers."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_Diagnose",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/code-change-review.bpmn#Task_Diagnose",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_codechangereview.task_implement",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Make the change"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The loop's only open-ended step. Everything around it is procedure; this is the work."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_Implement",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/code-change-review.bpmn#Task_Implement",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_codechangereview.task_preparemerge",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Prepare the merge, and watch it through"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "`prepare-merge` brings the base in, re-runs the gates and pushes — it does NOT merge. `watch` follows the PR until it is merged or closed, because webhooks do not reliably deliver CI success or a merge-conflict transition."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_PrepareMerge",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/code-change-review.bpmn#Task_PrepareMerge",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_codechangereview.task_review",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Review the change"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "A human or an agent acting AS reviewer. Nothing is a reviewer; somebody acts as one for the duration of this lane."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_Review",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/code-change-review.bpmn#Task_Review",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_codechangereview.task_runci",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Run the gates against the merge of head into base"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "CI tests the MERGE, not the branch. That is why a locally green tree can go red here: the agent's tree and the merge result are different trees, and the difference is invisible from a checkout."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_RunCI",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/code-change-review.bpmn#Task_RunCI",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_codechangereview.task_rungates",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Run the platform's own gates"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Before pushing, not after CI says so. `bun test` passing is NOT the gates passing: measured 2026-09-19, a green unit suite sat beside a `tsc` failure and a missing `@graphNode` tag, and the second broke a QA sidecar comparison as well — one cause, two symptoms, and an agent running only the tests would have pushed all three."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_RunGates",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/code-change-review.bpmn#Task_RunGates",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_codequalitygates.task_advisories",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Dependency advisories&#10;(WARN-ONLY)"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Asks the one question the lockfile cannot: is anything in the resolved tree KNOWN-VULNERABLE? Warn-only by the owner's ruling on bean `j41m` — a hard gate here would hand a transitive advisory nobody can patch the power to red every PR, and the suppression that follows is what rots. `.github/dependabot.yml` is the other half of that ruling and is NOT drawn here: it is not a job in this workflow, it runs on Dependabot's schedule."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_Advisories",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/code-quality-gates.bpmn#Task_Advisories",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_codequalitygates.task_e2e",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "End-to-end +&#10;accessibility (HARD)"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Install Chromium, check the rendered BPMN SVGs are current, then run the Playwright suite, which includes the accessibility checks. Hard: a failure blocks the PR."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_E2E",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/code-quality-gates.bpmn#Task_E2E",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_codequalitygates.task_lean",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Lean: no bare&#10;`import Mathlib` (HARD)"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Fail on any bare `import Mathlib` in content/**/*.lean — targeted imports only. In this platform repo there is no content/, so the job prints SKIP and states that nothing was scanned rather than passing silently."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_Lean",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/code-quality-gates.bpmn#Task_Lean",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_codequalitygates.task_python",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Python: unused and&#10;wildcard imports (HARD)"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "ruff F401 (unused) and F403 (wildcard) imports over the Python trees that exist, then the Python tests. A tree that is absent is dropped rather than passed to ruff, and an empty set says SKIP — a missing path must not be swallowed as a pass."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_Python",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/code-quality-gates.bpmn#Task_Python",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_codequalitygates.task_rust",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Rust wildcard imports&#10;(WARN-ONLY)"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Report non-test `use …::*;` in tools/**/*.rs, excluding `use super::*;`. continue-on-error: it reports and never blocks, which is why it is labelled WARN-ONLY rather than drawn like the hard jobs."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_Rust",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/code-quality-gates.bpmn#Task_Rust",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_codequalitygates.task_skillchain",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Skill-registration chain&#10;(UNMASKED)"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Runs the five `--check` commands that adding a skill stales, each on its own: gen-skill-docs, check:glossary, docs:auto:check, kg:audit:check, kg:detangle:check. A SEPARATE job rather than a step in Task_TypeScript, and that is the whole point of drawing it: every one of the five is already a step there, but all of them run after `bun test`, which executes the kg-audit and detangle WRITERS and so repairs two of the artefacts before their checks read them (bean `ymsu`). This job never runs `bun test`, so it is the only place those five are read against the tree as checked out. Measured 2026-09-26: 13s, and green on a clean tree. Drawn beside Task_Advisories rather than inside Task_TypeScript for a second reason — a red step placed BEFORE `bun test` would skip the 45 gates behind it, turning one named failure into forty-five unevaluated ones. Bean `v625` for why the chain needs a command at all; `fjwi` for the placement measurement."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_SkillChain",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/code-quality-gates.bpmn#Task_SkillChain",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_codequalitygates.task_typescript",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "TypeScript: tests, lint, types,&#10;and ~30 repository gates (HARD)"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "bun test, lint, tsc --noEmit, then the repository gates (workflow refs, lane and process documentation, kg:audit:check, detangle, skills, …). `bun run gates` derives its list from this job, so it is the local way to run the same set before pushing."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_TypeScript",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/code-quality-gates.bpmn#Task_TypeScript",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_codereview.task_recordverdict",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Record the verdict on the node"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Findings are advice, not commits — the same separation the generic reviewer lane keeps. Record them where the next reader meets the node."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_RecordVerdict",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/review-code.bpmn#Task_RecordVerdict",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_codereview.task_reviewschema",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Review the schema definition node"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Does the node declare what KIND of node it is? Does a widened type carry its mirrors? Does a removed field leave a reason behind, so the next author does not re-add it in good faith? And where the node RENDERS to something the site serves — a colour, a glyph, a theme's tokens — does a Tool maintain that artefact, and does the visual fact have only one home? The node decides; the stylesheet reports."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_ReviewSchema",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/review-code.bpmn#Task_ReviewSchema",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_codereview.task_reviewtool",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Review the Tool node"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Does it name skills, and do they resolve? Is the mechanism it advertises the one that actually runs? Are its IRIs minted rather than written out? And the question a covered skill hides: is the COMMAND reachable, or only the skill satisfied? A skill can be served by the neighbours of its mechanism while the mechanism itself is reachable from no node, and check:tools reports it as covered and is right to."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_ReviewTool",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/review-code.bpmn#Task_ReviewTool",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_codereview.task_runnodeaudits",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Run the node audits"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "`check:tools`, `kg:audit` and `typecheck`. Read the kg-qa sidecar rather than the summary: it is written per node so an inherited defect and a new one are distinguishable."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_RunNodeAudits",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/review-code.bpmn#Task_RunNodeAudits",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_contentacquisition.a_accept",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Accept it, and record where it came from"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Both branches land here. An unprompted offer is accepted as it stands — do not make somebody follow a process to hand over what they already have. Provenance is recorded whichever channel it arrived through: a description given in chat has a source and can be wrong, exactly as a PDF does."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_Accept",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/content-acquisition.bpmn#A_Accept",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_contentacquisition.a_ask",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Say what is needed, and ask for a link OR a description"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Both forms, named together. A person who cannot find the file often knows exactly what it is, and a description in their own words is an acquired resource rather than a consolation prize. Asking for the upload first demands the one thing they may not have, before the cheaper answers have been offered. Say what happens if they do nothing."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_Ask",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/content-acquisition.bpmn#A_Ask",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_contentacquisition.a_pointtoupload",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Point at the upload target [scripts/upload-url.ts]"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Composed from the declaration, never written by hand. The queue is declared with INSTANCE scope, so its declared path is missing the segment a repository-relative forge URL needs: /upload/main/uploads is a 404 and /upload/main/cat-harness/uploads is not, verified against GitHub 2026-09-20. Every failure is named — no origin remote, a non-GitHub forge, a declared-but-absent queue — because a URL is believed, and somebody sent to a wrong one cannot tell it from an empty directory. On failure, fall back to the conversation."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_PointToUpload",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/content-acquisition.bpmn#A_PointToUpload",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_contentacquisition.a_route",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Route it, and watch the queue"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "A file goes to ingestion; a link or a description goes to whatever will resolve it. Acquisition stops here — the moment a file is in the queue, library-ingestion owns it, and keeping that seam sharp is what lets a resource acquired through a channel that does not exist yet reach ingestion unchanged. An arrival may be minutes or days away, so it is watched rather than chased."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_Route",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/content-acquisition.bpmn#A_Route",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_contentacquisition.p_respond",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Give a link, a description, or neither"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "\"Or neither\" is a real outcome, not a failure. The ask says what happens if nothing comes, and then that happens — the work proceeds without the resource and says so."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "P_Respond",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/content-acquisition.bpmn#P_Respond",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_contentacquisition.p_upload",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Drop the file in the queue"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Through the forge's upload form, a commit, or any other route that lands the file in the declared queue. The agent watches rather than chases: an arrival may be minutes or days away."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "P_Upload",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/content-acquisition.bpmn#P_Upload",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_contentchangereview.call_adjudication",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Adjudicate the disagreement [adjudication]"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "adjudication.bpmn. When the editor and a reviewer, or two reviewers, disagree about a finding, an adjudicator settles it and records why; the review comment moves to `adjudicated` with the Decision that closed it. Permitted answers (bean `bvuk`, owner 2026-09-23): `stands` — the finding is right and the author addresses it; `withdrawn` — the finding is wrong and the comment closes. Recorded on the comment, not branched: either way the flow goes on to the coverage check."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Call_Adjudication",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/content-change-review.bpmn#Call_Adjudication",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_contentchangereview.call_optionsanalysis",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Options analysis how to absorb the impact"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "On the edge OUT of `Task_AssessImpact` and before `Task_CommitPush`, because the impact assessment is the evidence the options are weighed against. An analysis before it would compare ways of absorbing a downstream effect nobody has measured yet; one after the commit would be a rationalisation of a choice already pushed. NOT between `Task_AssessImpact` and `Task_ReviewImpact`, although that is the handoff the work-plan named. Those two tasks are in DIFFERENT LANES with no sequence flow between them — the agent's assessment reaches the committee through `Task_CompareBeforeAfter`, not directly — so there was no edge there to interpose on. The conceptual handoff is real; the edge was not. In the Agent lane, matching `upstream-version-adoption`: this step produces the options and their trade-offs, and `GW_Approved` in the Review Committee lane is where a decision is taken. A subprocess in the reviewer's lane would read as the committee analysing its own options, which is a different process. On the trigger: reaching this call is not the same as running the whole of it. `Process_OptionsAnalysis` opens with `A_Frame`, whose trigger is `opening-brief`'s — irreversibility and surprise, not size — and leaving at that first activity is a correct outcome rather than a skipped step. A copy-edit exits immediately; a logic change that moves an indicator does not, and this is the diagram where that distinction has teeth, since `Task_EditLogic` feeds straight into the assessment."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Call_OptionsAnalysis",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/content-change-review.bpmn#Call_OptionsAnalysis",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_contentchangereview.call_reviewslices",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Review each slice [review-task]"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "review-task.bpmn, once per slice, in parallel lanes by role. What kind of thing changed decides which review the slice descends into; the reviewer takes on that inner lane's role for the call only. Each reviewer gives the slice's blocks a verdict, and comments on the pull request with the `block:` tag where something needs saying."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Call_ReviewSlices",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/content-change-review.bpmn#Call_ReviewSlices",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_contentchangereview.task_approve",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Approve"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The committee approves the change: the judgement, recorded with the evidence it rests on. Approving is not merging. They were one task (\"Approve and merge\") until bean en2d split them, because a self-authored change cannot be approved through GitHub's own review (the approver may not be the PR's author), and a merge needs the owner's explicit confirmation whoever approved."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_Approve",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/content-change-review.bpmn#Task_Approve",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_contentchangereview.task_assessimpact",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Assess downstream impact"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Agent reviews downstream implications: - Will indicators need adjustment? - Will referral/follow-up for next visit be impacted? - Are translations affected (re-extract POT)? - Do Lean proofs still hold? skill: integration-watcher, translation-manager"
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_AssessImpact",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/content-change-review.bpmn#Task_AssessImpact",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_contentchangereview.task_buildstaging",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Build staging site"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "feature-staging.yml triggers: 1. Regenerate docs (schema, skills, content-backed pages) 2. Render BPMN diagrams 3. Stamp build with commit SHA + timestamp + branch 4. Build Jekyll site with STAGING/ baseurl 5. Inject yellow staging banner into every HTML page"
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_BuildStaging",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/content-change-review.bpmn#Task_BuildStaging",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_contentchangereview.task_cleanupstaging",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Remove STAGING/<slug>/"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "When the PR is merged or closed, the cleanup job removes the STAGING/<slug>/ directory from gh-pages so stale previews don't accumulate."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_CleanupStaging",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/content-change-review.bpmn#Task_CleanupStaging",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_contentchangereview.task_commentpr",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Comment staging URL on PR"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Bot comments or updates the staging URL on the PR. Includes commit SHA, branch name, and build log link."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_CommentPR",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/content-change-review.bpmn#Task_CommentPR",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_contentchangereview.task_commitpush",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Commit, push, update PR"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Agent commits all changes to the feature branch and pushes. The feature-staging.yml workflow automatically deploys to STAGING/<branch-slug>/ and comments the URL on the PR."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_CommitPush",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/content-change-review.bpmn#Task_CommitPush",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_contentchangereview.task_comparebeforeafter",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Compare main vs staging"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Review committee opens both URLs side by side: - Main site: <pages-url>/ (current published state) - Staging: <pages-url>/STAGING/<branch-slug>/ The staging banner shows the commit SHA so they can verify what they are reviewing matches the PR. A changed figure, diagram or table is also pictured before and after on the review page, with the share of changed pixels in words (skill visual-diff, Tool folio-block-screenshots)."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_CompareBeforeAfter",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/content-change-review.bpmn#Task_CompareBeforeAfter",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_contentchangereview.task_createbranch",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Create feature branch"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Agent creates a feature branch from main. Branch naming: feature/<short-description> Opens a PR immediately (AGENTS.md: \"open the PR at the first commit\")."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_CreateBranch",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/content-change-review.bpmn#Task_CreateBranch",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_contentchangereview.task_deploystaging",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Deploy to STAGING/<slug>/"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "peaceiris/actions-gh-pages deploys to gh-pages branch under STAGING/<branch-slug>/ with keep_files: true so other staging deployments and the main site are preserved."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_DeployStaging",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/content-change-review.bpmn#Task_DeployStaging",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_contentchangereview.task_describechange",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Describe the desired change"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Author describes the content change in natural language. Example: \"Update the immunization schedule to add a booster at 18 months.\""
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_DescribeChange",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/content-change-review.bpmn#Task_DescribeChange",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_contentchangereview.task_detectscope",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Detect change scope & impact"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Agent analyses the requested change: - Which content blocks are affected? - Are there downstream implications (indicators, referral logic, visit schedules)? - Will deterministic logic (CQL/DMN) need updating? skill: content-graph, integration-watcher"
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_DetectScope",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/content-change-review.bpmn#Task_DetectScope",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_contentchangereview.task_editcontent",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Edit narrative content blocks"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Agent modifies the relevant content blocks (.md files, block manifests). Validates each edit against the schema (content_validate). skill: content editing, block builders"
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_EditContent",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/content-change-review.bpmn#Task_EditContent",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_contentchangereview.task_editlogic",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Edit deterministic logic (if needed)"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "If the content change affects decision logic, indicators, or workflows: - Update CQL expressions - Update DMN decision tables - Adjust indicator definitions skill: dak-authoring, fhir-pipeline"
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_EditLogic",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/content-change-review.bpmn#Task_EditLogic",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_contentchangereview.task_ingestcomments",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Ingest tagged review comments [folio-review-comments]"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Every PR conversation comment that starts with `block: <label>` becomes a `folio-review-comment/v1` todo (open), idempotently, and is published with the preview as `review-comments.json`. The staging workflow runs this on every push and on every tagged comment; the coordinator owns that it has run before slicing, because the slices are cut around what reviewers have already said. This is the `ingest` transition of REVIEW_TRANSITIONS."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_IngestComments",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/content-change-review.bpmn#Task_IngestComments",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_contentchangereview.task_iterate",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Iterate on author feedback"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Agent receives revision requests from the author and applies changes. Each push triggers a new staging deployment with updated SHA stamp."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_Iterate",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/content-change-review.bpmn#Task_Iterate",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_contentchangereview.task_merge",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Merge, on explicit confirmation"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The owner says \"merge it\", and only then is the branch merged. Merge to main triggers: 1. the main site rebuilds with the changes; 2. the staging preview's cleanup runs; 3. the review comments committed on the feature branch land on main, as the review record."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_Merge",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/content-change-review.bpmn#Task_Merge",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_contentchangereview.task_rebuildmain",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Rebuild main site"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "docs-site.yml triggers on the merge commit to main, rebuilding the root of gh-pages with the accepted changes. The build SHA stamp now reflects the merged state."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_RebuildMain",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/content-change-review.bpmn#Task_RebuildMain",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_contentchangereview.task_requestchanges",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Request changes"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Committee provides feedback. PR stays open. Author and agent iterate further."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_RequestChanges",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/content-change-review.bpmn#Task_RequestChanges",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_contentchangereview.task_requestrevision",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Request further revisions"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Author provides feedback on what needs adjustment. Agent iterates on the feature branch."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_RequestRevision",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/content-change-review.bpmn#Task_RequestRevision",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_contentchangereview.task_reviewimpact",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Review impact assessment"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Committee reviews the agent's impact assessment: - Were all downstream effects identified? - Are the indicator changes acceptable? - Does the logic change match the narrative intent?"
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_ReviewImpact",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/content-change-review.bpmn#Task_ReviewImpact",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_contentchangereview.task_reviewstaging",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Review staged rendering"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Author reviews the rendered feature branch at <pages-url>/STAGING/<branch-slug>/ and compares against the main site. The staging banner shows the commit SHA."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_ReviewStaging",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/content-change-review.bpmn#Task_ReviewStaging",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_contentchangereview.task_sliceandassign",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Slice the change and assign reviewers"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "From the ChangeSet and the heat map on the review page: cut the change into slices a reviewer can hold (usually a section, or a run of sections where the heat map clusters), and assign each slice to a review lane by what it contains — clinical content to a clinical SME, a decision table to a QC reviewer, prose to a narrative reviewer. A block that needs no review (a pure rename, say) is WAIVED here with a written reason, which is what the coverage gate counts. Re-entered from GW_Covered when coverage is incomplete: the uncovered blocks become new slices."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_SliceAndAssign",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/content-change-review.bpmn#Task_SliceAndAssign",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_contentchangereview.task_submitforreview",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Submit to review committee"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Author submits the PR for formal review by the guidance review committee. The STAGING URL is the review surface."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_SubmitForReview",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/content-change-review.bpmn#Task_SubmitForReview",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_contentchangereview.task_watchbranchci",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Open the branch-watch bean [watch]"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "First dispatch point for a CI watcher: the feature branch has changed and a staging build now exists to watch. The watcher is DISPATCHED BY OPENING A BEAN, not by a workflow_dispatch -- per the owner on bean 29ij, this is a task/workflow initiation. That is the whole reason it is an activity rather than a line of prose. A bean makes the watch durable past the session that opened it: the container is reclaimed, and what survives is the claim. Starting the watcher and recording that it is running are ONE declared step, so the two cannot disagree about whether anything is watching. Claim rather than note: the watch is work in progress, and it is idempotent, so re-entering on a subsequent push does not duplicate it."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_WatchBranchCI",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/content-change-review.bpmn#Task_WatchBranchCI",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_contentchangereview.task_watchmainci",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Note the main-branch watch [watch]"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Second dispatch point: the change was approved and merged, and the root of the site has been rebuilt from main. This is the moment docs-site.yml failed all 30 times over two months (bean xom7) while looking exactly like a green run from inside the repo. `note` rather than `claim`, and the difference is not cosmetic. By here the branch-watch bean already exists, and whether the publish SUCCEEDED is a judgement this step cannot make -- the build reports its own exit code, and xom7 is the record of that being believed. AGENTS.md: a bean is not closed on someone else's say-so. So the step records what it observed and leaves the verdict to the watcher."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_WatchMainCI",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/content-change-review.bpmn#Task_WatchMainCI",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_contentchangereview.task_withdrawcomment",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Withdraw a review comment [folio-review-comment-move]"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The reviewer who made a comment takes it back (it was a misreading, or a later slice answered it). Recorded with `folio-review-comment-move --to withdrawn`, committed to the edit-set's feature branch like every status change. This is the `withdraw` transition of REVIEW_TRANSITIONS."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_WithdrawComment",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/content-change-review.bpmn#Task_WithdrawComment",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_copyoutmaterialized.task_editdirectly",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Edit it in place — it is your own content"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The ordinary path, drawn so the process does not read as though every edit needs a copy. Content in a writable directory is authored content and is edited where it lives; the copy-out is for somebody else's bytes, not for yours."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_EditDirectly",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/copy-out-materialized.bpmn#Task_EditDirectly",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_copyoutmaterialized.task_land",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Land the bytes in the copier's own folio/"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Into the copier's own declared `folio/`, never a scratch area — a directory nobody declared is a directory nobody gates, and the copy would be publishable by accident. The copy is NOT read-only: it is the copier's own content, makes no claim about anybody else's bytes, and freezing it too would mean the next person needs a copy of the copy."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_Land",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/copy-out-materialized.bpmn#Task_Land",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_copyoutmaterialized.task_readsource",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Read the original — and write nothing"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "A read, and the only interaction this process has with the source. Its digest and `provenance` are carried forward: the digest so Task_VerifySourceUntouched has something to check against, and `provenance` so the copy can name what it came out of without re-deriving it."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_ReadSource",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/copy-out-materialized.bpmn#Task_ReadSource",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_copyoutmaterialized.task_recordprovenance",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Record provenance.local — what this is a copy OF"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The step that is easy to omit and impossible to reconstruct afterwards. `provenance` is a PAIR: `upstream` is the remote thing, `local` is the original in this repository. A copy-out writes `local`; it does not overwrite `upstream`, and it does not reuse `upstream` for a local value — that was one field until 2026-09-22, and by then 5 of the 9 who-iris item records were using it for a local one in violation of its own documentation. Without `local`, one rename later the copy is indistinguishable from original work and nothing downstream can repair it, because the information was never written down."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_RecordProvenance",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/copy-out-materialized.bpmn#Task_RecordProvenance",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_copyoutmaterialized.task_verifysourceuntouched",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Verify the ORIGINAL still hashes to its digest"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "`check:materialized-fixity`. Run against the SOURCE, not the copy — the copy is new content with no claim to verify, and the source is the thing a botched copy-out would have disturbed. A mismatch here means the copy-out was an edit in place wearing a copy's clothes, and it is the only signal that tells the two apart."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_VerifySourceUntouched",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/copy-out-materialized.bpmn#Task_VerifySourceUntouched",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm.a_detect",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Detect feature request (crdm-detect skill)"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Recognise the request as a platform capability change rather than content work, from crdm-detect's signals. Never call it \"CRDM\" to the person. Mid-content-work, ask whether to pause for requirements now or record a bean for later — do not switch on your own."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_Detect",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-requirements.bpmn#A_Detect",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm.ba_submit",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Describe the need (chat, issue, discussion)"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The BA describes the capability gap in their own words. They do not need to know it is called CRDM."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "BA_Submit",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-requirements.bpmn#BA_Submit",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm.call_close",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Close-out"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The stakeholders sign off, the BA confirms every criterion is met, and only then does the agent close the issue. Never the other way round: an agent must never assume completion."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Call_Close",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-requirements.bpmn#Call_Close",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm.call_datamodel",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Data model Entities + cardinalities"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Between requirements and sign-off, and the order is the argument: requirements are statements about things, and the model says what the things ARE. Drafted earlier it is invented from nothing, since the entities come from the phase-2 BPA; drafted later, sign-off approves requirements whose nouns were never pinned — which is how two stakeholders approve one sentence meaning different things. Owner, 2026-09-20."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Call_DataModel",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-requirements.bpmn#Call_DataModel",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm.call_deliver",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Phase 6 Implement + acceptance"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "One phase and not three, because the loops say so: an increment the BA rejects, an MVP that is not ready, and stakeholder findings all route back into implementation. A subprocess has one exit and cannot be re-entered once finished, so splitting this region would have changed what the diagram says."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Call_Deliver",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-requirements.bpmn#Call_Deliver",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm.call_issue",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Link the work to an issue"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Feature work must be linked to a GitHub issue. Scan before creating, and never create one without the BA's permission — an issue is the stakeholder's record, not the agent's scratchpad."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Call_Issue",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-requirements.bpmn#Call_Issue",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm.call_needs",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Phase 1 Needs"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Identify the stakeholders, synthesise a needs statement from the sources, and loop until the BA and the stakeholders both recognise it. The loop is the phase: a needs statement nobody confirmed is an agent's summary, not a requirement."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Call_Needs",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-requirements.bpmn#Call_Needs",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm.call_requirements",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Phases 2–4 BPA + requirements"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Map the current workflow, then define the requirements and the impact they carry, and loop until approved. Same shape as Phase 1 and for the same reason: an unapproved requirement is a proposal."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Call_Requirements",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-requirements.bpmn#Call_Requirements",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm.call_signoff",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Phase 5 Beans + sign-off"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The approved requirements become work-plan items, the BA signs off, and the branch is announced on the issue. The announcement is on the single edge into delivery, so the three loops back into implementation do not re-announce."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Call_Signoff",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-requirements.bpmn#Call_Signoff",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm_close.a_close",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Close issue ONLY on BA authorisation"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Reachable only through BA_Confirm, which is the BA saying every criterion is met. An agent must never close an issue without that explicit authorisation — the gate is the preceding task, and this name says so rather than leaving a reader to trace the flow for it."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_Close",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-close.bpmn#A_Close",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm_close.ba_confirm",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Confirm all criteria met"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The business analyst confirms every acceptance criterion from the requirements is met. The issue closes only on their authorisation — an agent never closes an issue on its own say-so."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "BA_Confirm",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-close.bpmn#BA_Confirm",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm_close.s_featuresignoff",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Feature sign-off on issue"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Stakeholders sign off on the delivered feature on the issue, having tested the built artefact rather than a description of it."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "S_FeatureSignoff",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-close.bpmn#S_FeatureSignoff",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm_datamodel.a_declare",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Declare the model where a tool can read it"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "A model in prose is a proposal; a model in the declaration is a model. Ship a reader in the same change — everything here that was only documentation went inert within weeks."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_Declare",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-data-model.bpmn#A_Declare",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm_datamodel.a_entities",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Identify entities from the BPA and requirements"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Every verb in the BPA whose object is a candidate entity, and every noun in a requirement. An entity with no identifier is an attribute of something else — that test is decisive and belongs to the technique skill."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_Entities",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-data-model.bpmn#A_Entities",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm_datamodel.a_relations",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Relations and cardinalities, both ways"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Stated in both directions, because \"one attestation per report\" and \"one report per attestation\" are different claims and a model with only the first cannot say whether a re-signature is an update or a second row."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_Relations",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-data-model.bpmn#A_Relations",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm_datamodel.ba_confirmentities",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Confirm the entities are the ones meant"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "A naming question. The BA owns the domain vocabulary; the agent does not guess, which is CRDM's own rule for phase 1 and applies here with more force."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "BA_ConfirmEntities",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-data-model.bpmn#BA_ConfirmEntities",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm_datamodel.s_confirmcardinality",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Confirm the cardinalities"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "An operational question, asked of the people who run the process because they know where the exceptions are."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "S_ConfirmCardinality",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-data-model.bpmn#S_ConfirmCardinality",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm_deliver.a_codeaudit",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Audit the code nodes the increment adds"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Descend into the review task for what this increment CHANGED IN THE GRAPH — Tool definitions in `tools/` and schema definition nodes under `schemas/`. It runs before the summary, and therefore before an MVP can be shared: a Tool or schema node shipped in an MVP is the version stakeholders start building expectations on, and a node that names a skill nobody wrote is cheaper to catch here than after sign-off. Called, not inherited: the agent keeps its implementing role and takes on the `code-reviewer` lane inside Process_CodeReview for that call path only."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_CodeAudit",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-deliver.bpmn#A_CodeAudit",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm_deliver.a_deploystaging",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Deploy the MVP to staging"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "An MVP is shared AS A STAGING DEPLOY, not as a description of one. `feature-staging.yml` publishes the branch under `STAGING/<branch-slug>/` on gh-pages and comments the URL on the PR, so the stakeholder who tests it is looking at the built artefact rather than at a screenshot — the same argument the merge discipline makes about rendered work. Measured in this repo on 2026-09-16: holding a rendered change back for assessment made assessment harder, not safer."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_DeployStaging",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-deliver.bpmn#A_DeployStaging",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm_deliver.a_implement",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Phase 6: Implement (feature branch + PR)"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Inner loop: agent claims a bean, implements on feature branch, opens PR, posts summary to the issue."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_Implement",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-deliver.bpmn#A_Implement",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm_deliver.a_summary",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Post summary to issue"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "What was accomplished, what remains, and links to the updated content for review."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_Summary",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-deliver.bpmn#A_Summary",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm_deliver.ba_reviewincrement",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Review increment (test behaviour)"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Inner loop: the BA tests each delivered increment against the acceptance criteria. They do not review code — they test behaviour."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "BA_ReviewIncrement",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-deliver.bpmn#BA_ReviewIncrement",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm_deliver.ba_sharemvp",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Share MVP with stakeholders"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Outer loop: the BA presents the accumulated increments to stakeholders as a testable MVP. Staging URL, demo, or walkthrough."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "BA_ShareMVP",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-deliver.bpmn#BA_ShareMVP",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm_deliver.ba_translatefeedback",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Translate feedback into agent direction"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The BA translates stakeholder findings into actionable direction: new beans or bean updates for the agent."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "BA_TranslateFeedback",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-deliver.bpmn#BA_TranslateFeedback",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm_deliver.call_optionsanalysis",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Options analysis how to implement"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "On the single edge from `Start_Process_CRDM_Deliver` into `A_Implement`, so the approach is chosen before any code exists. By Phase 6 the needs, requirements and data model are signed off, which is exactly the evidence an options analysis needs and the reason it belongs here rather than earlier: at `Call_Needs` there is nothing to weigh, and after `A_Implement` the choice has been made in code. Note where this is NOT. The work-plan named `crdm-requirements-workflow`, and `A_Implement` is not in that diagram — `crdm-requirements.bpmn` is the orchestrator, seven call activities and a gateway, and Phase 6 lives here in `crdm-deliver.bpmn`. The call goes where the step is, not where the plan said to look. The three loop-backs into `A_Implement` — `_5` (increment rejected), `_7` (MVP not ready), `_13` (feedback translated) — deliberately BYPASS this call. Routing them through it would run the subprocess on every iteration of the inner loop, which is the ceremony this design refuses: a gate invoked on every pass stops being read. An iteration reworks an approach already chosen; if the APPROACH is what is wrong, that is not a loop iteration and it belongs to the calling step in `crdm-requirements.bpmn`. Contrast `upstream-version-adoption`, where the loop DOES re-enter the analysis. There the loop-back returns to `A_Impact`, which re-gathers the evidence, so the second pass weighs genuinely different inputs. Here the loop returns to implementation with the evidence unchanged. `A_Implement` carries `cat-harness.processes:bean op=\"claim\"`; this step carries no bean op, because `Process_OptionsAnalysis` ends with its own `decision-audit` note on the bean the caller claimed."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Call_OptionsAnalysis",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-deliver.bpmn#Call_OptionsAnalysis",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm_deliver.s_testmvp",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Test MVP in own context"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Stakeholders test the delivered feature in their own workflow, with their own data. They report what works and what does not."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "S_TestMVP",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-deliver.bpmn#S_TestMVP",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm_issue.a_askcreate",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Ask BA to create or link issue"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Ask — never create. Creating an issue without the BA's permission is the thing this step exists to prevent."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_AskCreate",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-issue-linking.bpmn#A_AskCreate",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm_issue.a_linkissue",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Link to existing issue"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "A match was found: ask the person whether the requirements go on #NNN, then link the work there. The issue is where stakeholders sign off, so no phase proceeds without one."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_LinkIssue",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-issue-linking.bpmn#A_LinkIssue",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm_issue.a_scanissues",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Scan open issues for match"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Search open issues, then recently closed ones, by title and body keywords for one this request belongs to. Requirements may span several issues; note every relevant one."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_ScanIssues",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-issue-linking.bpmn#A_ScanIssues",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm_issue.call_relatedwork",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Related work: find, sort, ask"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "When the requirement is initiated or updated through a human-agent chat, search the beans and the repository's issues and open PRs for relevance, categorize and summarize them, and ask the user whether and how to coordinate. Judgement decides the categories; the user decides the coordination. Owner, 2026-09-23 (issue #1023)."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Call_RelatedWork",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-issue-linking.bpmn#Call_RelatedWork",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm_needs.a_stakeholders",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Phase 1: Identify stakeholders"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The agent asks the BA who is affected by this change. The BA knows the domain — the agent does not guess."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_Stakeholders",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-needs.bpmn#A_Stakeholders",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm_needs.a_synthesise",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Phase 1: Synthesise needs from sources"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "From the chat, issue, uploads and library sources, write a clear, jargon-free statement of what is needed and why, tied to a concrete workflow. Post it on the GitHub issue, not in chat, and ask the requester and stakeholders to review it."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_Synthesise",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-needs.bpmn#A_Synthesise",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm_needs.ba_reviewneeds",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Review synthesised needs statement"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The BA reviews what the agent synthesised and checks it against what they actually need."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "BA_ReviewNeeds",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-needs.bpmn#BA_ReviewNeeds",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm_needs.s_confirmneeds",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Confirm needs statement"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Stakeholders confirm, on the issue, that the needs statement says what they need — or say what to change. A stakeholder's judgement; an agent does not record it for them."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "S_ConfirmNeeds",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-needs.bpmn#S_ConfirmNeeds",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm_requirements.a_compareoptions",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Phase 4a: Compare the viable options"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Phase 4 often ends with a CHOICE rather than a plan, and this is the step that hands it over. Per option: what it does, its pro, its con, what it changes DOWNSTREAM, and how reversible it is — laid out where the rows can be read against each other, then one recommendation and a stated default. A step of its own rather than a line inside A_DefineReqs, because it has a different output and a different reader: the impact analysis is for the record, the comparison is the thing the BA answers from. Folding it in is how it gets skipped — the analysis feels finished, so the options go over as a list of names. Skipped legitimately when the analysis yields ONE viable approach. Do not manufacture alternatives to fill a table."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_CompareOptions",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-requirements-definition.bpmn#A_CompareOptions",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm_requirements.a_definereqs",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Phases 3–4: Define requirements + impact"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Two skills, because this step is two things: the requirements come from the CRDM process, the impact half is a dependency question the content graph answers."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_DefineReqs",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-requirements-definition.bpmn#A_DefineReqs",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm_requirements.a_mapworkflow",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Phase 2: Map current workflow (BPA)"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Business-process analysis here means reading the existing diagrams under processes/ and drawing the gap, so the skill that implements this step is the BPMN one."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_MapWorkflow",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-requirements-definition.bpmn#A_MapWorkflow",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm_requirements.ba_reviewreqs",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Review requirements and impact analysis"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The BA reviews the formal requirements and the impact analysis the agent produced."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "BA_ReviewReqs",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-requirements-definition.bpmn#BA_ReviewReqs",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm_requirements.s_approvereqs",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Approve requirements"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Stakeholders approve the requirements and impact analysis on the issue, or send them back for revision. Only their approval moves the work to sign-off; an agent never records an approval on a person's behalf."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "S_ApproveReqs",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-requirements-definition.bpmn#S_ApproveReqs",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm_signoff.a_announcebranch",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Announce the branch on the issue"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "On CREATING the feature branch, comment on the issue: the branch name, the process and phase, and the beans claimed. Visibility is the whole point — without it a sibling session or a human cannot tell that work has begun, only that it has finished. Deliberately on this edge and not inside Phase 6. The three loops back into A_Implement (increment rejected, MVP not ready, feedback translated) re-enter implementation on the SAME branch, and re-announcing on each would be noise. Announce once, when the branch is created."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_AnnounceBranch",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-signoff.bpmn#A_AnnounceBranch",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm_signoff.a_createbeans",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Phase 5: Create beans"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The agent mints the implementation beans itself with `beans create`, running the exact-title existence check first. The engine has no `create` op — it claims, notes and resolves the instance's OWN bean — so what this step records here is a note that the plan now exists."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_CreateBeans",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-signoff.bpmn#A_CreateBeans",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm_signoff.a_offerkg",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Offer the knowledge-graph destinations for the agreed set"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "THE STEP THAT WAS MISSING. Requirements were elicited, agreed and signed off, and then existed as an issue and a conversation — so the output of the process that exists to produce durable requirements was the one thing the knowledge graph never learned. ONE question for the SET, not one per requirement: a six-phase run can agree many, and asking six times is the same failure as a form that re-asks what it was already told. The options are DERIVED from the graphs this instance declares in `<name>.json`, read at the time of asking, so an instance that adds a graph gets it in the offer without anybody editing a skill. Never a list typed from memory."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_OfferKg",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-signoff.bpmn#A_OfferKg",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm_signoff.a_recordkg",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Run placement, and raise a bean for the authoring"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The offer produces a DECISION, not a node. `placement` then decides instance, graph and node kind — it is the step that catches a hardcoded path or a literal naming one folio — and the authoring itself becomes a bean, because work here is a bean before it is a file. `op=\"note\"` and not `create`, for the reason `A_CreateBeans` above states: the engine has no `create` op — it claims, notes and resolves the instance's OWN bean. The agent mints the authoring bean itself with `beans create`, running the exact-title existence check first, and what this step records is a note that the decision was taken."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_RecordKg",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-signoff.bpmn#A_RecordKg",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm_signoff.ba_choosekg",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Choose a destination, or none"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "A PERSON'S STEP, and `none` is one of the answers rather than a refusal to answer. A requirement whose whole content is carried by the code becomes a commit and nothing else; a graph that acquires a node for it is a graph with a node nobody will ever read. The default creates NOTHING. An agent that decides on its own that a requirement \"is really a skill\" has manufactured a node nobody asked for, in a graph somebody else maintains — which is what this step exists to prevent."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "BA_ChooseKg",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-signoff.bpmn#BA_ChooseKg",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_crdm_signoff.ba_signoff",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Sign off on requirements"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The business analyst / requester signs off on the agreed requirement set, on the issue: what was agreed and what was deferred. Recorded as their decision, with its reason, never by an agent on their behalf."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "BA_Signoff",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/crdm-signoff.bpmn#BA_Signoff",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_criterionadjudication.a_dispensation",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Grant a dispensation, with its reason"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The rule applies and this subject is a stated exception. A `kind: \"human\"` entry with `result: \"pass\"` overrides the script's `fail` for that criterion, and ONLY while its `field_hash` matches the current source — so the dispensation is scoped to the version it was granted against, lapses when the block changes, and never becomes precedent. There is nothing to overturn later; the source moving overturns it. A dispensation with no `notes` is not a dispensation. It is an override somebody applied to get to green, and nobody can review it afterwards — which is why this step is not relaxable."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_Dispensation",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/criterion-adjudication.bpmn#A_Dispensation",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_criterionadjudication.a_recordentry",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Write the entry that LEADS — keeping the checker's beneath it"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Not relaxable, and the one step here that is not. A judgement nobody wrote down is indistinguishable from a checker that was never run, so the judgement is free and the record is not. Do not resolve the disagreement away: both entries stay, the adjudication on top under the sweep's most-recent-matching-hash rule. A disagreement between a checker and a reviewer is information, and somebody re-running the check next month needs to find that a checker read it differently rather than a clean pass. `/api/relevance/adjudicate` reached the same rule independently — `human_adjudicated` written alongside, never over, the agent's `assessed_by`."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_RecordEntry",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/criterion-adjudication.bpmn#A_RecordEntry",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_criterionadjudication.a_scopecriterion",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Scope the criterion so it stops applying here"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "One edit to the criterion rather than ten overrules on the blocks it should never have covered. This branch is the one an adjudicator under time pressure converts into a dispensation, and the conversion is a defect: a dispensation lapses when the source moves, so a mis-scoped criterion granted its way past comes back every time anybody touches the block."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "A_ScopeCriterion",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/criterion-adjudication.bpmn#A_ScopeCriterion",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_criterionadjudication.call_adjudicate",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Adjudicate the criterion disagreement"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The shared judgement — entry condition, untainted dispatch, person-or-agent restriction — asked with THIS question's permitted answers. `cat-harness.processes:adjudication codes` sits here rather than on `A_Adjudicate` inside it because the answers depend on what was asked, and the gateway below is what acts on them: the engine refuses a mismatch between the two. `Process_Adjudication` may also leave at `End_NotAdjudicable` — one entry and no other side is a review or a gate, not a disagreement — in which case nothing below runs and there is nothing to record."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Call_Adjudicate",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/criterion-adjudication.bpmn#Call_Adjudicate",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_derivecontent.task_archive",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
