        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Task_Validate",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/authoring-a-document.bpmn#Task_Validate",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_editing.call_optionsanalysis",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Options analysis accept · revise · discard"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "On the edge out of `Task_ReviewFindings` and before `Task_RecordDecision`: the findings are the evidence, so the options can only be weighed once they exist, and after `Task_RecordDecision` the decision is already written down. NOT between `Gateway_EditorDecision` and `Task_RecordDecision`, which is the pair the work-plan named — in this diagram those run the OTHER WAY ROUND. `Flow_21b` goes `Task_RecordDecision` -> `Gateway_EditorDecision`, so the gateway reads a decision that has already been recorded, and interposing there would analyse options after the choice was made. In the Agent lane, and this diagram makes the reason sharp. `Task_RecordDecision` is a `userTask` in `Lane_Editor` that already names `decision-audit`, and `Process_OptionsAnalysis` ends with its own `decision-audit` note. Those are two different acts — the subprocess records that the options were WEIGHED, the editor records WHAT WAS CHOSEN — and putting the analysis in the editor's lane would collapse them, making the same party both analyse and decide. The subprocess's own documentation refuses that: it produces options and a recommendation, and the authorisation belongs to the calling step. `CallActivity_Evidence` sits in `Lane_Editor` instead, and that is not an inconsistency: the author performs the evidence retrieval, whereas here the point is that the analyst is not the decider. On the trigger: `A_Frame` opens the subprocess on `opening-brief`'s trigger — irreversibility and surprise — and leaving there is a correct outcome. A spelling fix that reached `Task_ReviewFindings` with one mechanical finding exits immediately; a revise-or-discard on a block other content depends on does not."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "Call_OptionsAnalysis",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/editing-hci-validation.bpmn#Call_OptionsAnalysis",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_editing.callactivity_evidence",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Gather and verify the evidence [evidence-retrieval]"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Before anything is drafted: the author reads the guidance ALREADY in this content, frames the question as PICO, retrieves candidates across the three evidence classes, and has each candidate's authority resolved against its publisher's own API. A recommendation reaches the drafting step with its evidence attached, or with the gap recorded. This step has nothing to do for content that carries no recommendations -- a mathematics folio has none -- and is skipped there rather than satisfied vacuously."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "CallActivity_Evidence",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/processes/editing-hci-validation.bpmn#CallActivity_Evidence",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/ns#glossary/kg-bpmn-activities/process_editing.task_agentreview",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
