      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "See ingest-l1-completeness-gate.bpmn. NOT YET SKILL-BACKED. This step named `paper-relevance-triage`, which has never existed, and is not `proof-triage` (that one triages proofs). Left uncovered until the skill is written. The gate contains one adjudication (Task_FlagDrift: `real`, `spurious` or `source-wrong`), and its own Task_Verdict records the answer as a reason against the verdict before returning. So both answers reach this step, and nothing here branches on them; Gateway_Complete branches on the gate's completeness verdict instead."
        }
